<title>SLOVAKIA: SLOVAK JAN 1997 CURRENT ACCOUNT DEFICIT $230.3 MLN. [CORRECTED 09:35 GMT]</title>
<headline>SLOVAK JAN 1997 CURRENT ACCOUNT DEFICIT $230.3 MLN. [CORRECTED 09:35 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Slovak current account recorded a deficit of $230.3 million (corrects from $203.3 million) in January 1997, compared with a shortfall of $19.6 million in January 1996 and a full year 1996 deficit of $1.94 billion, the National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) said in its February monetary survey obtained by Reuters on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The survey did not include figures for the January capital account.  </p>
<p>SLOVAK CURRENT ACCOUNT     JAN 1997   JAN 1996	FY/1996</p>
<p>  overall ($ million)	  -230.3     -19.6	 -1,940.8</p>
<p>  trade balance		  -227.7     -50.2	 -2,105.8</p>
<p>  balance of services	    +1.0     +11.5	     +7.4</p>
<p>  income balance		   -9.6	+9.0	    -44.7</p>
<p>  current transfers		+6.0     +10.1	   +202.3</p>
<p> -- Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-521-8402</p>
